{"parseRefreshTokenResponse overwrites missing refresh tokens with placeholder 'refresh_token' string, which will clobber valid refresh tokens downstream and break future refreshes": 0.8791942000389099, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses [z.string().toString()] which yields a literal key and makes it required, so real token payloads will fail validation": 0.9188305735588074, "googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts stores entire parseRefreshTokenResponse wrapper object as credential key instead of extracting .data property": 0.986763060092926, "refreshOAuthTokens returns a Response object when credential sharing is enabled but returns refreshFunction() result otherwise - callers expect .data property which doesn't exist on Response objects": 0.9228485822677612, "zoho-bigin/lib/CalendarService.ts passes credentialId instead of credential.userId to refreshOAuthTokens, causing sync to target wrong subject": 0.9761493802070618, "No response validation in refreshOAuthTokens - the fetch response status and content aren't checked": 0.7784631252288818, "salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts uses stale credentialKey values when creating jsforce connection instead of refreshed token values": 0.9312434196472168, "appCredentialWebhookRequestBodySchema.parse can throw on invalid payload, turning bad input into 500s instead of 400s": 0.9173009395599365, "Handler accepts any HTTP method but should enforce POST with a 405 response like other webhook handlers": 0.6674861311912537, "Header lookup is case-sensitive - if CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME is set in mixed case, lookup will fail because Node.js normalizes incoming headers to lowercase": 0.7664399147033691, "Header lookup doesn't handle arrays - if the header is sent multiple times, req.headers[...] will be an array and comparison against a string will incorrectly allow the request through": 0.2798998951911926, "JSON.parse(symmetricDecrypt(...)) can throw on decrypt/JSON errors, turning bad input into 500s instead of 400s": 0.8780539631843567, "No error handling for the fetch call in refreshOAuthTokens - network failures throw unhandled exceptions": 0.7115173935890198, "No timeout on the external fetch in refreshOAuthTokens, risking indefinite hangs": 0.5518543124198914, "The () => any type signature in refreshOAuthTokens provides no type safety": 0.0073245819658041, "Missing prisma import in salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts for credential update": 0.9343570470809937, "zohocrm/lib/CalendarService.ts caller expects AxiosResponse with .data property but refreshOAuthTokens can return fetch Response, causing runtime error": 0.9503610730171204, "Read-then-write pattern for credential upsert can create duplicates under concurrent requests without unique constraint": 0.8761160373687744}